      "writtenOn": "2025-03-14T15:43:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I was also asked during Chrome Rust sync-up meeting if changing how `kMedium` works may even further regress the compression ratio.  I think the short answer right now is: not necessarily / we don\u0027t know.  The longer answer is:\n\n* Before this CL `kMedium` would use the `flate2` backend.  After this CL `kMedium` will use the `fdeflate` backend (+ adaptive filters, unlike `kLow` which will use `fdeflate` with hardcoded `Up` filter).\n* [The docs](https://github.com/image-rs/image-png/blob/eb9b5d7f371b88f15aaca6a8d21c58b86c400d76/src/common.rs#L333-L335) for `kFast` say that it \"Significantly outperforms libpng and other popular encoders by using a [specialized DEFLATE implementation tuned for PNG](https://crates.io/crates/fdeflate), while still providing better compression ratio than the fastest modes of other encoders.\"\n* I guess this CL is an attempt to quantify/measure these documentation claims and compare to what we got in previous Canary+Dev trials.",
